  "response": "UNDER TEMPORARY CODEX FAILOVER MODE\n\n# Security Remediation Roadmap\n\nThis report constitutes the architectural review and remediation roadmap for the `fluentwithkyle/openclaw-webhook` repository. \n\nAs requested, NO files have been modified, NO commits created, and NO changes pushed.\n\n---\n\n## Complete Security Audit Status Summary\n\n| # | Item | Status |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| 1 | Google Apps Script Authentication | DONE |\n| 2 | Tally Webhook Authentication | NOT DONE |\n| 3 | Cal.com Webhook Authentication | NOT DONE |\n| 4 | Logging Minimization & Privacy | PARTIALLY DONE |\n| 5 | Configuration & Secret Hygiene | PARTIALLY DONE |\n| 6 | Sensitive Information in Artifacts | NOT DONE |\n| 7 | Full Git History Secret Scan | NOT DONE |\n| 8 | Webhook Input Validation | REVIEW REQUIRED |\n| 9 | Apps Script Privilege Review | REVIEW REQUIRED |\n| 10| Deployment/Access Configuration | REVIEW REQUIRED |\n\n---\n\n## Remediation Roadmap\n\n### Priority 1 — Critical / Immediate\n\n#### 1. Tally & Cal.com Webhook Authentication\n*   **Finding:** Webhooks receive unauthenticated requests. An attacker could flood the system with fake intake or booking data, triggering CRM updates and LINE notifications.\n*   **Files Involved:** `index.js`, `services/tally.js`, `services/cal.js`.\n*   **Proposed Approach:** \n    *   **Tally:** Verify if Tally supports signature verification (usually HMAC-SHA256). If yes, implement verification middleware in `index.js` or within `handleTallyWebhook`.\n    *   **Cal.com:** Verify if Cal.com supports signature verification. If yes, implement similar middleware in `index.js` or `handleCalWebhook`.\n*   **Dependencies:** Provider documentation for webhook security mechanisms.\n*   **Configuration:** New Render environment variables for Tally/Cal.com webhook secrets.\n*   **Testing:** Simulate signed and unsigned requests to verify rejection of invalid/missing signatures.\n\n#### 2. Logging Minimization\n*   **Finding:** `index.js` logs the *entire* inbound webhook body for Tally and Cal.com using `JSON.stringify(req.body, null, 2)`. This potentially logs sensitive PII (names, emails, line IDs) and guest information.\n*   **Files Involved:** `index.js`.\n*   **Proposed Approach:** Remove full body logging. Replace with structured, sanitized logging: event type, timestamp, event ID (if available), and action status (success/failure).\n*   **Testing:** Verify via logs (after deployment) that PII is no longer exposed.\n\n---\n\n### Priority 2 — High\n\n#### 3. Configuration Hygiene (Spreadsheet ID)\n*   **Finding:** `google-apps-script/CRM.js` has a hardcoded `SHEET_ID`.\n*   **Files Involved:** `google-apps-script/CRM.js`.\n*   **Proposed Approach:** Move `SHEET_ID` to Google Apps Script Script Properties (`CRM_SHEET_ID`) and update `CRM.js` to retrieve it via `PropertiesService`.\n*   **Manual Config:** Configure `CRM_SHEET_ID` in Apps Script Script Properties.\n*   **Testing:** Verify `getSheet()` still correctly opens the spreadsheet.\n\n#### 4. Webhook Input Validation\n*   **Finding:** Webhook handlers (`services/tally.js`, `services/cal.js`) process payloads with minimal schema validation before acting on them (CRM upserts, email sending).\n*   **Files Involved:** `services/tally.js`, `services/cal.js`.\n*   **Proposed Approach:** Define a required schema for Tally and Cal.com payloads. Reject requests missing mandatory fields before processing begins.\n*   **Testing:** Unit test handlers with malformed/incomplete payloads.\n\n---\n\n### Priority 3 — Medium\n\n#### 5. Apps Script Privilege Review\n*   **Finding:** The Apps Script web app executes as the deploying user with full access to Sheets and Gmail.\n*   **Files Involved:** `google-apps-script/appsscript.json`.\n*   **Proposed Approach:** Audit the manifest for necessary OAuth scopes. Ensure only the absolute minimum required permissions remain.\n*   **Testing:** Ensure functionality remains after scope restriction.\n\n#### 6. Deployment and Access Configuration\n*   **Finding:** Potential for obsolete deployments.\n*   **Proposed Approach:** Ensure only the intended App Script URL is active and known to Render. Rotate secrets if they were exposed in old configurations.\n\n---\n\n### Priority 4 — Low / Cleanup\n\n#### 7. Artifact Cleanup\n*   **Finding:** `gemini-artifacts/` may contain logs with sensitive data.\n*   **Proposed Approach:** Analyze `gemini-artifacts/` content. If sensitive, remove these files from the repository immediately. Add `gemini-artifacts/*.log` to `.gitignore`.\n\n#### 8. Full Git History Secret Scan\n*   **Finding:** Potential historical exposure of secrets.\n*   **Proposed Approach:** Use a tool like `trufflehog` or `git-secrets` to scan the complete repository history locally. If secrets are found: Rotate/Revoke, then remove from history (e.g., via `git filter-repo` or BFG), then force-push.\n*   **Rollback:** This is destructive; have a full backup before history rewriting.\n\n---\n\n## RECOMMENDED EXECUTION ORDER\n\n1.  **Stop full-body logging in `index.js`** (Highest PII impact, easiest to fix).\n2.  **Move `SHEET_ID` to Apps Script Script Properties** (Clean up hardcoded secrets).\n3.  **Implement webhook signature verification** for Tally and Cal.com (Requires provider research and secret management).\n4.  **Implement strict input validation** in `tally.js` and `cal.js`.\n5.  **Audit and clean repository artifacts** (Add to `.gitignore`).\n6.  **Full Git history scan.**\n7.  **Apps Script Privilege/Deployment Review.**\n\n---\n\n## FINAL REPORT SUMMARY\n\n*   **Remediated:** Google Apps Script Shared Secret Authentication (Verified).\n*   **Vulnerable:** Inbound webhook processing (unauthenticated and over-logged), hardcoded Spreadsheet ID, unmanaged logs.\n*   **Next Actionable Task:** Stop logging full webhook bodies in `index.js`.\n*   **Blocker:** Research into Tally/Cal.com signature verification mechanisms is required before implementation.\n*   **Manual Action:** Kyle must configure `CRM_SHEET_ID` in Apps Script Script Properties once the `CRM.js` update is approved.\n\nReport completed under **TEMPORARY CODEX FAILOVER MODE**.",
